    "documents": [
      {
        "id": "system-guide",
        "title": "Reading the system",
        "format": "markdown",
        "attachments": [
          {
            "kind": "graph",
            "ref": "order-processing"
          }
        ],
        "markdown": "# Reading this system\n\nThis is a **fictional, partial model** of the current Order Processing system.\nIt explains what is established about order submission and what remains open.\n\n## Two implemented routes\n\nCheckout API can submit to Fulfillment directly, or publish an order submission\nthat Order Worker consumes before calling Fulfillment. The model does **not**\nestablish which route is primary, which is a fallback, or whether they are exclusive.\n\nRead the [worker guide](../services/worker/README.md) and the\n[submission details](../interfaces/submission.md#route-selection).\n\n| Question | Recorded state |\n|---|---|\n| Does the worker consume from Order Queue? | Established |\n| What selects each submission route? | Unknown |\n| Who approves production deployments of the worker? | Disputed |\n\n## How to read the arrows\n\nArrows describe operations from actor to resource. For consumption, the\n[worker](#node=order-worker) points to the queue it consumes from.\nPosition does not establish execution order.\n\n> These documents explain the fixture. Their attachment does not make every\n> sentence a separately validated architectural claim.\n\n[Return to the graph](#graph=order-processing).\n",
        "links": [
          {
            "href": "../services/worker/README.md",
            "target": {
              "kind": "document",
              "ref": "worker-guide"
            }
          },
          {
            "href": "../interfaces/submission.md#route-selection",
            "target": {
              "kind": "document",
              "ref": "submission-details",
              "heading": "route-selection"
            }
          },
          {
            "href": "#node=order-worker",
            "target": {
              "kind": "node",
              "ref": "order-worker"
            }
          },
          {
            "href": "#graph=order-processing",
            "target": {
              "kind": "graph",
              "ref": "order-processing"
            }
          }
        ],
        "assets": []
      },
      {
        "id": "worker-guide",
        "title": "Order Worker guide",
        "format": "markdown",
        "attachments": [
          {
            "kind": "node",
            "ref": "order-worker"
          }
        ],
        "markdown": "# Order Worker\n\nThe worker consumes order submissions from Order Queue and calls Fulfillment.\nIts internal functions and replica count are outside this diagram's scope.\n\n## Responsibilities\n\n1. Consume a queued order submission.\n2. Submit the order to Fulfillment.\n\nThis list describes the fixture's responsibilities. It does not specify retries,\nidempotency, timing guarantees, or concurrency between orders.\n\nRead [submission details](../../interfaces/submission.md) or inspect the\n[worker-to-Fulfillment relationship](#edge=worker-submit).\n\n## Ownership remains disputed\n\nCommerce and Operations report different owners for the same exclusive deployment\napproval responsibility, environment, and snapshot. Neither report has been\nselected as established ownership.\n\n## Example vocabulary\n\n```json\n{\n  \"from\": \"order-worker\",\n  \"kind\": \"consumes\",\n  \"to\": \"order-queue\"\n}\n```\n\nThis is a relationship excerpt, not a complete model or a wire protocol contract.\n\nSee the [system guide](../../guides/system.md#two-implemented-routes).\n",
        "links": [
          {
            "href": "../../interfaces/submission.md",
            "target": {
              "kind": "document",
              "ref": "submission-details"
            }
          },
          {
            "href": "#edge=worker-submit",
            "target": {
              "kind": "edge",
              "ref": "worker-submit"
            }
          },
          {
            "href": "../../guides/system.md#two-implemented-routes",
            "target": {
              "kind": "document",
              "ref": "system-guide",
              "heading": "two-implemented-routes"
            }
          }
        ],
        "assets": []
      },
      {
        "id": "submission-details",
        "title": "Submission details",
        "format": "markdown",
        "attachments": [
          {
            "kind": "edge",
            "ref": "worker-submit"
          },
          {
            "kind": "edge",
            "ref": "direct-submit"
          }
        ],
        "markdown": "# Submission details\n\nBoth [Checkout API](#node=checkout-api) and [Order Worker](#node=order-worker)\nhave implemented calls to Fulfillment in this fictional snapshot.\n\n## Route selection\n\nThe selection conditions for the direct and queued routes are **unknown**.\nWhether one order can take both routes is also unknown. No primary/fallback\ndescription is established.\n\n## Interface details\n\nThe fixture does not supply the request schema, endpoint path, authentication\nmechanism, response codes, or retry contract. This document deliberately leaves\nthose unspecified rather than inventing a plausible API.\n\nAn actual interface contract could be written in an ordinary document like this;\nthe tool does not treat contracts as a special type.\n\n[Read the worker guide](../services/worker/README.md#responsibilities).\n",
        "links": [
          {
            "href": "#node=checkout-api",
            "target": {
              "kind": "node",
              "ref": "checkout-api"
            }
          },
          {
